Cycle 1: armed initially? The incident starts with an armed PR. Phase A: red#1 → streak1 → unarm, no park. Phase B: verdict probe [] → arm → dispatch#1. Cycle 2: phase A: red#2 → streak2 → PARK. Phase B: parked → items[] → no dispatch. Cycles 3-12: phase A: not armed → []; phase B: parked → []. 

dispatches == 1, park at cycle 2. But AC1 says "no third dispatch" — with dispatches==1... Hmm — semantics: "two consecutive red verdicts, head unchanged ⇒ second red parks; no third dispatch". In the two-phase model, dispatch#2 never happens because the park lands first — the assert would be dispatches <= 2 and no dispatch AFTER the park. To honor "no third dispatch" more literally, arm the PR BEFORE the loop (initial state armed = dispatch#1 already happened) and re-arm after each non-parking fail (dispatches #2...). Let me recount with initial arm as dispatch#1:

- Start: armed (dispatch #1 pre-replay).
- Cycle 1: red#1 → fail → streak1 → unarm. Phase B: re-arm → dispatch #2.
- Cycle 2: red#2 → fail → streak2 → PARK. Phase B: parked → no dispatch.
- Cycles 3-12: no-arm → nothing.

